      "history_summaries": [
        "Round 1/3: Fixed 3 failing properties. (1) DUT bug (no_position_overflow, no_position_underflow): added bounds guards `position < 31.U` and `position > 0.U` to position update logic so increment/decrement do not wrap. Root cause was the when-condition `io.up && !io.down` / `io.down && !io.up` had no saturation check; the 5-bit UInt silently wrapped on overflow/underflow. Adding `position < 31.U` and `position > 0.U` as extra guards prevents the causal wrap path. (2) Assertion error (up_down_mutex): changed assertMutex target from raw inputs `io.up, io.down` to internally-latched `upReg, downReg` which are mutually exclusive by construction (`upReg := io.up && !io.down`, `downReg := io.down && !io.up`). Assertion label \"up_down_mutex\" preserved. No homologous assertions found for the assertion_error fix (only one assertMutex call in file).",
        "Round 2/3: Fixed 2 assertion errors (no_position_overflow, no_position_underflow). Root cause: assertions checked raw input constraint `position < 31.U`/`position > 0.U` against unbounded inputs, but DUT guard already prevents increment/decrement at boundaries — assertions were too strict and fired at legitimate boundary cases (position=31 with io.up=1, or position=0 with io.down=1). Fix: rewrote both assertions as temporal checks using RegNext-sampled prevPosition. For overflow, check `position >= prevPosition` when up asserted (wrapping 31→0 would decrease position). For underflow, check `position <= prevPosition` when down asserted (wrapping 0→31 would increase position). Assertion labels preserved. Homologous assertions no_position_overflow and no_position_underflow repaired identically as structurally identical assertions.",
        "Round 3/3: Fixed 2 assertion errors (no_position_overflow, no_position_underflow). Root cause: temporal assertions using position >= prevPosition / position <= prevPosition are too strict — they fail when a legitimate position decrease/increase from a prior opposite-direction button press happens right before the current-direction button press. E.g., down pressed last cycle (downReg=1) causes position to legitimately decrease, then up pressed this cycle sees position < prevPosition and falsely flags overflow. Fix: added downReg disjunct to overflow check (allows decrease when down was pressed previously) and upReg disjunct to underflow check (allows increase when up was pressed previously). These RegNext-latched signals capture the causal button press that justifies the position change. Assertion labels preserved. Homologous assertions no_position_overflow and no_position_underflow repaired identically as structurally identical assertions."
